  "title": "Dendron",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "82dd5f9a-5f9b-4623-ba58-a95d40e8fb08",
      "text": "A dendron is a basic receptive unit of the cerebral cortex: a bundle or cluster of up to about 100 apical dendrites of the pyramidal cells of laminae V and III-II, as they ascend to lamina I, receiving up to 100,000 spine synapses. There are about 40 million dendrons in the human cerebral cortex.",
